{"name":"Template","hex":"#a6c9e3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"template","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A physical object whose shape is used as a guide to make other objects.","A generic model or pattern from which other objects are based or derived."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set up or mark off using a template.","To provide a template or pattern for."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/template"}],"entries":[{"title":"Die (manufacturing)","blocks":[{"text":"A die is a specialized machine tool used in manufacturing industries to cut and/or form material to a desired shape or profile. Stamping dies are used with a press, as opposed to drawing dies and casting dies which are not. Like molds, dies are generally customized to the item they are used to create."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Die_(manufacturing)"},{"title":"Molding (process)","blocks":[{"text":"Molding or moulding is the process of manufacturing by shaping liquid or pliable raw material using a rigid frame called a mold or matrix. This itself may have been made using a pattern or model of the final object."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Bronze_spearhead_mold.JPG/330px-Bronze_spearhead_mold.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Molding_(process)"},{"title":"Template (C++)","blocks":[{"text":"Templates are a feature of the C++ programming language that allow functions and classes to operate with generic types. This allows a function or class declaration to reference via a generic variable another different class without creating a full declaration for each of these different classes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_(C%2B%2B)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/ProgressiveDieToyota-strip-scrap.jpg/500px-ProgressiveDieToyota-strip-scrap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped